title: Two-way GitHub sync — COMPLETE (CLI + web + background poll, end-to-end)
summary: 'Finished the true two-way GitHub sync Matt asked for. Outbound: CLI verbs (start/done/shelve/edit --reopen) + web write verbs (claim/start/done/block/unblock) project transitions to the linked issue (close/reopen/label) best-effort. Inbound: `paradigm task sync`, POST /api/tasks/sync, and a 120s background poll in `paradigm serve` all reconcile linked issues back through the SAME enforced writers (a pull never bypasses assertTransition). The web GitHub strip is now a real Sync button (summary + clickable conflicts + calm offline hint) and the board live-refreshes off the tasks:synced WS broadcast. The full visceral loop works: drag→Done closes the issue; a teammate closing/reopening the issue moves the card through the enforced state machine. Local stays canonical; conflicts surface, never force. Build green CLI 441 / MCP 468.'
