  - portal.yaml
  - CHANGELOG.md
learnings:
  - The whole two-way feature stayed safe because EVERY mutation — outbound projection, inbound reconcile, CLI, web, poll — routes through one enforced seam (updateTask/completeTask/shelveTask). Five trigger surfaces, one write path. The reconcile brain is pure and the sync-layer is the only writer, so 'a pull can't bypass enforcement' is provable, not asserted.
  - Outbound projection is fire-and-forget at the call sites that ALREADY own the enforced write (CLI verbs + web router), never inside updateTask — keeping the loader pure (no provider import) and avoiding firing on the recursive blocked_on auto-clear write. The local write commits first; gh is best-effort after.
  - The background poll lives in the platform server (the one long-running process), unref'd + non-overlapping + env-disablable — a poll belongs in serve, not the loader or a standing daemon, and only runs while the UI is up.
